<title>SOUTH KOREA: Seoul to raise foreign shr holding limit on Oct 1.</title>
<headline>Seoul to raise foreign shr holding limit on Oct 1.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea will raise the foreign share ownership limit to 20 percent from the current 18 percent on October 1, the Finance Ministry said on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>The foreign share holding limit on state-owned Korea Electric Power Corp and Pohang Iron and Steel Co would be expanded to 15 percent from the current 12 percent, it added.</p>
<p>Individual foreign shareholders would be allowed to hold up to five percent of a stock, from four percent at present.</p>
<p>Individual holdings in state-owned companies will remain unchanged at one percent.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5644</p>
